  "_africa_pilot_doc": "v17 (2026-07): Africa is a SMALL, HIGH-RISK pilot restricted to desert/subtropical hub cities only (Cairo, Casablanca, Algiers, Tunis, Johannesburg). Two safeguards distinguish these from the EU stations: (1) resolution_source='metar' routes force_resolution_sweep to REAL station observations via aviationweather.gov instead of the Open-Meteo ERA5 archive (ERA5 bias in Africa exceeds the 1C market tick and there is NO regional forecast model on the continent); if the METAR is unavailable the market stays UNRESOLVED rather than falling back to ERA5. (2) pilot=true forces every proposal through the full LLM judge (never deterministic auto-approve) and marks it high-risk. The bot fences the rest of Africa (lat -35..37, lon -18..52) with a discovery skip 'africa_non_pilot' — the monsoon/ITCZ belt (Lagos/Accra/Dakar/Addis/Nairobi) is explicitly NOT operated (forecast skill collapses and the resolution truth is unreliable there). No om_models: no regional model exists, so the global trio (icon/gfs/ecmwf) is used.",
  "_station_names_doc": "v9: map of station name phrases (as they appear in Polymarket market descriptions) to ICAO codes that exist in the 'stations' dict above. Used by auto_extract_station_from_description to resolve markets where the operator hasn't yet curated the city. Keys are lowercased phrases; auto-extractor strips 'Station', 'Airport', 'the', 'International' etc before lookup.",
